    "title": "Somali President Rejects Israeli Presence, Warns Against Regional Conflicts",
    "original_title": "Mdaxweyne Xasan Sheekh: Soomaaliya ma Aqbali doonto joogitaanka Israa’iil ee Dalka",
    "slug": "somali-president-rejects-israeli-presence-warns-against-regional-conflicts",
    "summary": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud states Somalia will not accept any Israeli military presence, citing reports of a planned base in Berbera. He also vows to prevent Somalia from being drawn into Middle East tensions.",
    "content": "Somali President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud has declared that Somalia will not permit any Israeli military presence on its territory under any circumstances. In an interview with Al Jazeera, he also affirmed that his government would oppose any efforts to involve Somalia in the conflicts and tensions affecting the Middle East.\n\nThe president's remarks come amid reports that Israel is planning to establish a naval military base in the coastal city of Berbera and to utilize the city's airport. Berbera, located in the self-declared republic of Somaliland, has been at the center of recent geopolitical interest due to its strategic location near the Gulf of Aden.\n\nThis development follows a 2024 memorandum of understanding between Ethiopia and Somaliland, which granted Ethiopia access to the sea in exchange for potential recognition. Somalia strongly opposed that deal, viewing it as a violation of its sovereignty. The reported Israeli plans add another layer to the complex regional dynamics.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this stance underscores the government's commitment to protecting national sovereignty and avoiding entanglement in broader Middle Eastern conflicts. Many in the diaspora have expressed concerns about external interference in Somali affairs, and the president's statement may resonate with those who prioritize stability and independence.\n\nSomalia has long maintained a policy of non-alignment in regional disputes, and the president's comments reaffirm that position. The international community is closely monitoring the situation, as any military presence in Berbera could significantly alter the security landscape of the Horn of Africa.\n\nThe Somali government has not provided further details on how it plans to prevent such a presence, but the president's firm rejection signals a potential diplomatic confrontation if the plans proceed.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/04/mdaxweyne-xasan-sheekh-soomaaliya-ma-aqbali-doonto-joogitaanka-israaiil-ee-dalka/",
